t(61, 1255, """The great tree is the Prophet ﷺ. The dream foretold events in the dominion of Allah the Almighty, our Lord, and changes in His dominion; hallowed are His names and attributes, and He is exalted in the heavens and on earth, most highly exalted. The great tree sprouting quickly means very rapid events occurring in the world that will bring the great tree back to the forefront once more, so that the light of the Muhammadan message shines anew once again

A dream from a few months before the war .. The dreamer is from the Strip

She says: I saw a comet in the sky, and it was daytime. Beside the star the moon was clear and big and its light was strong. I started saying "Subhan Allah, what is going to happen?" and I was very amazed. Suddenly the world lit up with a strong white light, and a beautiful green tree began to sprout, its leaves shining, and it was growing quickly. It stopped at a certain height, but it was high, beautiful and tall. Suddenly the world lit up with light again, and after it a green tree sprouted beside the great tree, but it did not reach the height of the first tree, and it was as if it came from its root. I was greatly amazed and said: "Glory be to You in Your dominion." End.

The first Muhammadan tree sprouted with the noble prophetic mission, and this was a "light", as in the dreamer's words "a strong white light". For the Prophet ﷺ is a manifestation of the will of Allah the Almighty to illuminate the earth and bring it and its people out of darkness. Likewise the noble Muhammadan message was a light that encompassed the earth and its people and came from heaven; so the earth shone with the light of its Lord, and the Muhammadan message was activated because of this light .. Then there will be a light upon the earth at the end of time, illuminating the earth anew with justice and truth and reactivating the noble Muhammadan message. So the sprouting of the first great Muhammadan tree is due to the light of the Almighty Lord, hallowed be His names; this light illuminated the earth and shone upon it to activate the Muhammadan message. And the sprouting of the shorter tree at the end of time, with the branch rising to reactivate the role of the root, is likewise caused by the light of our Almighty Lord manifesting upon the earth from our Lord, hallowed be His names, so that He permits the role of the root to be reactivated as it was, through the branch.""")

t(63, 115, """Unfortunately, however disciplined the channels are, nonsense is sure to occur in them, and this pushes brothers to contact me privately to ask; I find a general answer better than a private one .. A question came to me about the claim of a dream-interpretation channel that the Imam does not pray at night out of fear of the devils! While Allah the Exalted is calling him to the night prayer .. They speak on behalf of Allah the Exalted about an unseen matter they have no knowledge of, based on nothing but a wrong interpretation and a mistaken reading of dream symbols! I do not know the extent of this audacity toward Allah the Exalted?! Then at another time they say: he does not pray at night out of laziness, and they interpret the dreams wrongly so as to come out to people with wrong words .. I do not know why the ethic of "I do not know" has vanished from our Ummah?! It is better for a person to say I do not know, and these people do not know that interpreting dreams is a fatwa. Very many of us pray at night, so what about the Imam?! If among all of us many pray at night and many of us strive, then what about that man?! Where is the mind of these interpreters? Where did they forget it? They must have forgotten it somewhere and never gone back to fetch it! One of the strangest of things is that very many of us Muslims pray at night, while that person, about whom they made dozens of claims, whom they pelted with much slander, and to whom they attributed every possible defect, that person does not pray at night. At one time the very same person comes out and says he is being lazy, and at another time that he is afraid of the devils so that they do not recognise him! By Allah, a nonsense in which no one in all the worlds preceded them; I just do not know what their minds are made of or how they are put together! We pray at night and that man does not pray at night, afraid of the devils lest they recognise him, so he does not pray at night and does not draw near to his Lord out of fear of the devils! He does not pray at night while I, you and millions of Muslims do?!! By Allah, shame! Do they not feel a little ashamed?! A little shame, by Allah, would spare them people's mockery and keep people from scorning their weary minds. Be ashamed for your own sakes, not for anyone else! Be ashamed, if only so that you are not an object of people's mockery and of criticism for the size of your small minds that come out with such statements, which neither religion nor reason nor logic accepts. You use dreams in a wrong interpretation, decode a symbol in the dream 100% wrongly, and broadcast that wrong understanding to people? Does everyone who says "I am an interpreter" become, overnight, like Allah's prophet Yusuf? Put the possibility of your error in your mind and measure your wrong interpretation against much of the known information; you will realise that you are on a road opposite to the correct interpretation! This, unfortunately, is the state of YouTube channels, and unfortunately even those with a good amount of wisdom and reason go astray like this, as if devils possess their owners from time to time!""")

t(63, 1480, """Life's journey has carried us along .. and we have alighted at our last abode .. and seen the true beauty of the earth .. and revelled in the blessings of Allah the Almighty before we go to Him .. May we depart having been forgiven""")

t(64, 480, """Abundant water""")

t(64, 1910, """Hold firm; however great the weariness, it is not forever! It will pass and be only a painful memory! It will be the fuel that ignited your new self! That set it free! That released from it the beast that lay hidden in you! The beast to which you always used to say: I am ashamed of your existence! It was not a shame .. It was a necessity for this hard time, but you did not know .. and did not understand .. and did not feel .. You were coming from afar .. You were coming from an age that was never born, not even once, in the course of humanity! You were coming from the age of illusion that you yourself made in your mind .. You were living your own world .. your own way .. You were besieging yourself by yourself .. shooting your arrows at your own walls with both hands .. and releasing your beasts to devour you .. and burning your tents with your own fire, not your enemy's fire .. and making a thousand catapults every day to batter down every stone of your will .. You were the enemy .. You were the pain .. and you were your own aches .. You were your own enemy .. And you were killing all your friends within yourself .. crushing them .. annihilating them .. capturing them .. chaining them and violating them without mercy .. So weariness came to you to break all your arrows .. to burn all your illusions, to expose all your naivety, and to demolish your whole path that was filled with your tears and sighs .. To expose you before yourself .. Those tears and sighs that you thought were your honour, your dignity and the proof of your humanity .. All of that was a lie, an illusion, and nothing but forbidden sacrifices!

"And be patient until Allah judges, for He is the best of judges" """)

t(65, 1490, """Once upon a time there was something in the world called the Net .. But a young generation today is still living its childhood .. Tomorrow it will ask for many walking tours .. And this intelligence draws, by the decree of Allah the Almighty, what the heart wishes to see of children, even with an imprecise description of what is wanted!""")

t(66, 540, """O dim light: how many eyes grew drowsy early because of you .. For people's next day matters .. Because people have become human once again, anew""")

t(66, 2010, """In the last age .. warmth .. "The Line of the last era" .. Whenever the river said "I am here", timbers were lowered and nails were hammered .. Because it is the last era .. the era of the beautiful farewell to the earth""")

t(67, 1005, """Life without safety has no value .. Yet how many a person is secured and safe and still does not see the blessing!""")

t(67, 2420, """A river stretching on .. so what about all the cities on its bank?!""")

t(68, 1380, """The Prophet ﷺ said: "People are just like a hundred camels; you can hardly find among them one fit to ride."
Narrator: Abdullah ibn Umar | Scholar: al-Bukhari | Source: Sahih al-Bukhari

The meaning is that most people are people of deficiency, self-interest, desire for lusts and desire to worship whim. As for the people of virtue, their number is very small; they are like the riding camel among the pack camels: one in every 100. And even this single riding camel is precious, rare; you can hardly find it among 100 souls!

In this hadith is a statement of the rarity of the people of truth, the rarity of those who follow the truth, and the rarity of those through whom truth is upheld on earth""")

t(69, 710, """The larger the population in a contiguous geopolitical space, the more recycling plants are effective in the economy .. economising .. helpful .. and a lever for the economy .. Because they are plants that benefit from people's consumption of recyclable products and their reuse in industry, and from reducing the cost of raw materials from primary sources""")

t(69, 2260, """For 100 years people have suffered from the crowding of the big government institutions, where people from all districts and neighbourhoods gather, stand in long queues and spend long hours inside one large government complex, unlike other countries that developed and made a government building for each neighbourhood, serving only its residents, so people do not pile up and do not stand in long queues""")

t(70, 1325, """China .. The world's largest shipbuilder by number every year""")

t(71, 250, """I was not the only one who felt anguish and pain and whose tears poured down after hearing the story of the orphan Majd, 14 years old, whom the "teacher" beat, so he said to him: If Dad were alive you would not have hit me!

A sentence that shook the consciences of many people .. A sentence that breaks the human soul, shakes the spirit and sets off in consciences an unexpected and unbearable storm .. A phrase that must shake everyone and must put everyone before their responsibilities .. These children in schools are not fair game to be assaulted in the way that happened to Majd .. Discipline in schools was and still is a festering file in the Islamic world, especially in state schools .. A festering file, and the crisis of this file can only be solved through laws, and through cameras inside the classrooms, between the classrooms and in every place inside the schools""")

t(71, 2090, """Cities of the Victorian era .. Their neighbourhoods suggest the warmth of man's relationship with man""")

t(72, 1000, """Mount Moriah""")

t(73, 1350, """We are a whole generation, and with us the generation of the grandfathers, the generation of the fathers and the generation of the sons .. 4 generations have paid the price of the injustice of those who ideologised injustice and legislated it as replacement in a land that has never been empty since the dawn of history .. When you break a cup, do not expect anyone to pay its price on your behalf, and when you break a soul, never expect it to smile at you!""")

t(74, 265, """Wars are not a game, killing people is not a game, occupying the lands of others is not a game, and brutalising peoples under the yoke of replacement and substitution is not a game. And when a conflict begins anywhere in this world and an unarmed people is brutalised, and then the days of the world turn and time turns, what began as no game does not end like a game! What began and was not a game cannot end as though it had been a game!""")

t(74, 1890, """A dream published today on one of the forums: The dreamer says: "I saw the account of a man called (Abdullah) whom I do not know; he was looking at Jerusalem with a furtive glance and reciting the noble verses: "He said: I am the servant of Allah; He has given me the Scripture and made me a prophet (30) and He has made me blessed wherever I am and has enjoined on me prayer and zakah as long as I live (31)" The dreamer is from Gaza .. February 2026

If the dream is true, then the descent of Allah's prophet Isa, peace be upon him, has drawn near, and Allah knows best""")

t(75, 1150, """A dream published today on one of the forums .. The dreamer saw the dream in the middle of last Rajab .. The dreamer says: "I was in the old family house in Gaza .. I saw that the sky was raining heavily on Gaza. It was night, the tents were flooding and the people were exhausted. Suddenly the rain stopped over Gaza. It was as if I was watching the world from the balcony of the house. The rain continued over other areas outside Gaza. Suddenly the moon turned into a sun in the dead of night, and then went back to a full moon (this was repeated 3 times). And I felt the warmth of the sun. Words I did not understand were appearing on the moon. But I started screaming and saying: "This is a sign of the Mahdi's appearance", and I was saying in the dream: here we are in mid-Rajab, and in Ramadan a sign will come that everyone will see and be sure that the Mahdi is going to come. I started crying a lot and saying Allahu Akbar, and I prostrated in thanks to Allah out of joy. End

Interpretation of part of the dream: If the dream is true, the matter is 3 years after the distress of the Strip, and Allah the Exalted knows best""")

t(76, 540, """Oneness with the noble Muhammadan message, and not merely following it!
The one who is united and merged with the noble Muhammadan message is a person who is jealous for the Almighty, Most High, Holy Essence of Allah, hallowed be His names and attributes. The one merged with the noble Muhammadan message does not accept anything in which there is even a suspicion of offence to Allah the Exalted; he erupts like a volcano that never dies down. Or he is jealous for the Prophet ﷺ or for the prophets of Allah the Almighty, peace and blessings be upon them, or he is jealous for what the Almighty Lord commanded and what He forbade; so he does not allow a wrong idea to pass, even if he himself is insulted, even if he is accused of falsehood, even if things are said about him that mountains could not bear by way of abuse!

The greatest terror is to approach a monotheist who is jealous for Allah the Almighty, not one who merely loves Allah the Exalted! Not one who merely obeys Allah the Exalted! Otherwise there would not be this warning, which I deliver with the utmost gravity; it is a statement after understanding, an understanding that comes only today, at this time, after long years of observation and reflection .. As for the one united with the noble Muhammadan Shari'ah, do not approach him with harm .. Because Allah the Exalted will be angry for his sake when he is wronged, humiliated, mocked or not respected. And the terror of approaching one who has united with the noble Muhammadan Shari'ah is because this servant has reached the degree of jealousy for Allah the Exalted .. He is jealous for Allah the Almighty .. The problem of approaching him with harm is not like the problem of approaching the righteous, for the righteous are one thing and the one who is jealous for Allah is another. The degree of jealousy for Allah is the degree of siddiqiyyah (utmost truthfulness), not the degree of righteousness! And siddiqiyyah is not attained and no one reaches it except when his certainty in the Almighty Lord is completed by witnessing, not only by thought and feeling! And the one jealous for Allah witnessed the signs and proofs with his own eyes only because he was jealous for Allah in fact, not in imagination or supposition. As for the righteous one, he ascends the ranks of reforming the self out of love or awe! But the one who is jealous for Allah the Exalted has passed the stage of ascending through hope or awe. The one who is jealous for Allah the Exalted has united with the noble Muhammadan message and become a part of it, not a mere follower of it. For the one who is jealous for Allah the Exalted considers that the Muhammadan message is not merely a message sent down to legislate right and wrong; rather it is a personal desire, as though he desired it in the world of pre-existence before he was created, and wished for it while in the world of the unseen. So when he was born and learned that the noble Muhammadan message had indeed come before his birth, he did not look, at the stage of reaching the rank of "jealousy", he did not look at it when he reached that rank, he did not look at it as only legislation!

The one who is jealous for Allah the Exalted has an innate jealousy for the Essence of Allah the Exalted before he knows of the Shari'ah and its existence. He is jealous for the Essence of Allah the Exalted, which he came to know from the Muhammadan Shari'ah itself, but his love for Allah the Exalted did not make him live on earth merely applying the Shari'ah and what it brought. Rather, his love for Allah the Exalted made between him and Allah the Exalted a relationship that is not made through the Shari'ah alone; it is made on the foundation of the pure, noble Muhammadan Shari'ah, and then jealousy for Allah is built in the soul, the building of the special relationship between the servant and his Lord. It is a relationship that is not made by the qualities of the righteous alone (that does not happen), for righteousness in itself does not lead to that rare, special, chosen path; it is made only in anger for Allah the Almighty, for His Messenger, for His prophets, for His servants and for His creation, the weak among them, then the weak, then the weak.

There, only in that place abandoned by most people, there love is melted down, not to remain mere love but to become something else, different; it becomes a complete, perfect allegiance with no breach in it. And complete allegiance to Allah the Almighty is not like the righteousness of the soul, its return, its repentance and its commitment. Allegiance to Allah the Almighty, our Lord, means complete fusion and complete merging with His will on earth, and it means complete loyalty to the noble Muhammadan message, not merely following it, acting on it, and moving between its path and the paths of Satan, rising and falling.

Complete allegiance to Allah the Exalted means that on earth you are jealous for Allah the Almighty, not for yourself. You are jealous for Allah the Almighty, not for your children! You are jealous for Allah the Almighty, not for your parents, your siblings, your husband, your wife or your relatives! You are jealous for Allah the Almighty in everything. You are jealous for Allah the Almighty as though Allah the Exalted has charged you, as a Muslim monotheist, to walk upon this earth, whatever your colour or origin, as a representative of the noble Muhammadan message; you take it with strength, you take the Book with strength, and you do not waver, because it is Allah the Exalted, the Almighty, who willed""")

t(77, 60, """this Muhammadan message, sent it down and commanded that it be followed!

Your jealousy for Allah, while He is able to punish everyone who offends Him, and He is able to punish everyone who angers Him, and He is able to do whatever He wills with the wrongdoers, and He does not need your anger for Him, nor does He need your jealousy for Him. Yet despite knowing all that, you are jealous for Him, knowing that He has no need; nevertheless you are jealous for Him! This is oneness with the will of Allah the Exalted on earth, and not merely following the noble Muhammadan message. And this jealousy means that Allah the Exalted is, in your heart, singled out above all that is singled out and sought above all that is sought, and that the relationship with Him is desired above every relationship with any other. This jealousy, which Allah the Exalted never needs from anyone, is the highest representation of your love for Him .. your anger for His sake .. After people, except those on whom our Lord has mercy, have come to be angry only for themselves .. and jealous only for their possessions .. and do not see Allah the Exalted above everything .. but see everything in this world and its goods above everything.""")

t(77, 840, """It is called the Capital""")

t(77, 2315, """It is called the Capital""")

t(78, 1270, """The Capital .. in Ramadan .. This is how Istanbul used to be called .. Then, in this way, Jerusalem inherits the same name after 100 years""")
